<section class="home-section handoffs" id="handoffs">
  <div class="home-wrap">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <p class="mono-kicker">WHERE IT BREAKS</p>
      <h2>Work moves across the dealership.<br><span>The money leaks at the handoffs.</span></h2>
      <p>The systems inside a dealership can each be doing what they were designed to do while the operation between them still breaks down.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="handoff-layout">
      <div class="handoff-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="flow-card active" data-flow="0"><span>MARKETING</span><i></i><span>BDC</span><i class="broken"></i><span>SALES</span><b>WAITING</b></div>
        <div class="flow-card" data-flow="1"><span>ACQUIRED</span><i></i><span>RECON</span><i class="broken"></i><span>READY</span><b>NEXT ACTION ?</b></div>
        <div class="flow-card" data-flow="2"><span>FINANCE</span><i></i><span>BILLING</span><i></i><span>ACCOUNTING</span><b>EXCEPTION / OWNER —</b></div>
        <div class="flow-card" data-flow="3"><span>SERVICE</span><i class="broken long"></i><span>SALES</span><b>HANDOFF LOST</b></div>
      </div>
      <div class="handoff-stories">
        <article class="handoff-story active" data-flow="0"><span>01</span><h3>A lead waits for a response.</h3><p>Marketing creates the opportunity. The next action doesn't happen fast enough.</p></article>
        <article class="handoff-story" data-flow="1"><span>02</span><h3>A vehicle waits for the next step in recon.</h3><p>The work exists. Ownership of the next handoff is unclear.</p></article>
        <article class="handoff-story" data-flow="2"><span>03</span><h3>A funding exception sits unnoticed.</h3><p>The information is in the operation, but the right person can't see what needs attention.</p></article>
        <article class="handoff-story" data-flow="3"><span>04</span><h3>A service opportunity never reaches Sales.</h3><p>The signal exists. The workflow connecting it to action doesn't.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="handoff-verdict"><p>The problem isn't always the technology.</p><h2>It's often what happens between it.</h2></div>
  </div>
</section>

